1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,267
What if Earth stopped—

2
00:00:01,533 --> 00:00:02,233
right now?

3
00:00:02,633 --> 00:00:03,567
At the equator,

4
00:00:03,567 --> 00:00:04,533
you’re already moving

5
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:05,333
about a thousand

6
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:06,333
miles an hour.

7
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,333
You don’t feel it

8
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:08,767
because  you, the ground,

9
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,500
and the air move together.

10
00:00:10,633 --> 00:00:12,000
Stop the ground suddenly,

11
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:13,000
and loose objects

12
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,900
initially keep moving east.

13
00:00:14,867 --> 00:00:16,367
The air keeps going too.

14
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:17,867
And so does the ocean.

15
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:19,000
Closer to the poles,

16
00:00:19,033 --> 00:00:20,700
that starting speed is lower.

17
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:22,533
The stop is imaginary.

18
00:00:22,633 --> 00:00:24,400
The motion is real.

